---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import PageHeader from "@oblivios/site-shared/components/PageHeader.astro";
import Print from "@oblivios/site-shared/components/Print.astro";
import { sources } from "../lib/site.mjs";

sources("devices", [
  "Daily phone, calls, SIM and camera, Compartments: the owner's statement of 2026-11-18 (decision 256, 257, 258).",
  "docs/devices/support-policy.md (Pixel 10a bring-up record: Personal Stable, personal data allowed, relocked with the project key; the entry gate for a supported device)",
  "docs/quality/validation-matrix.md STALLION-001 (relock), STALLION-002, 006, 007, 008, 009 (updates through the updater; the read of 2026-11-09 on candidate 2026110503: user build, yellow and locked, packages airpods, datamap, exit, guardian, passwords), STALLION-004 (Duress core scenarios)",
  "AIR-197 (candidate 2026100501 through the updater, AirPods stack)",
  "docs/product/status-app-surfaces.md (the app drawer and the keyboard on stallion since the candidates named there)",
  "docs/product/status-privacy-and-identity.md and docs/release/build-log.md (the Pixel 7a has no SIM)",
  "Decision 112 (the independent rebuild is deferred)",
  "The images paragraph is the owner's intention of 2026-11-18 (decision 256).",
]);
---
<Page
  title="Devices: ObliviOS"
  description="Which phones run ObliviOS today: the Pixel 10a I use every day and the Pixel 7a I develop on. No device is supported yet, and what has to be true before one is."
  path="/devices"
  current="/devices"
>
  <PageHeader crumb="Devices" title="Devices" lede="Which phones run ObliviOS, which one I use every day, and what has to be true before I call any of them supported.">
    <Print id="ph" label="Two phones, one large and one small" />
  </PageHeader>
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="c lead">
      <div>
        <p class="big">No device is supported. Two phones run ObliviOS builds: the Pixel 10a I use every day, and the Pixel 7a I develop on.</p>
        <p class="fn">ObliviOS is source only: there is no image to flash.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="c gap-top">
      <dl class="kv">
        <dt>Pixel 10a <code>stallion</code></dt>
        <dd>My daily phone, with my personal data on it. Calls, the SIM and the camera work on it. Its bootloader is locked with my own key, so verified boot reads yellow and locked, and it takes signed updates through the system updater: six so far, the latest read on 9 November 2026. It runs Compartments, Network exit, Atlas, Duress Unlock, Passwords, the app drawer, the keyboard and AirPods support.</dd>
        <dt>Pixel 7a <code>lynx</code></dt>
        <dd>My development phone and the first engineering target. New work is built and checked here first. It has no SIM card, so calls and mobile data are not tested on it.</dd>
        <dt>Supported</dt>
        <dd>No device. A device counts as supported only after it passes the entry gate below.</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band">
    <div class="c">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What supported means</h2>
        <p>A device is supported only with verified upstream device source, current firmware and driver coverage, a monthly update path, signed images and updates, locked-bootloader verification, recovery validation, and evidence for emergency and radio functions. A booting image alone is not support, and a phone that I use myself is not a support claim.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="c">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Images</h2>
        <p>If real interest in ObliviOS shows, I want to publish images for the Pixel 10a. I have not set a date. Before I do, the five gates of a public beta on the <a href="/status">status page</a> have to be met. One more thing stands in the way, and I postponed it on purpose: nobody has rebuilt a signed image independently and compared it byte for byte (decision 112). I decide on the day, separately. Until then ObliviOS is source only.</p>
        <div class="callout"><h3>No date, no promise</h3><p>Nothing on this page says that an image will exist. It says what I intend and what stands in the way.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
